WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.040
Look, the bottom line here, Meg, is that
you're just taking your own problems out on

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:04.970
everyone else.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.650
Oh, my problems?

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:11.630
Oh, I see. Is this coming from my role model
mother? The shoplifter, the drug addict, the

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:15.560
porn star, the whore who let Gene Simmons and
Bill Clinton go to town on her?

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.120
Oh, so what?

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:22.160
All those things are behind me now. I'm a
better person now because of those experiences.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:24.200
Are you are you a better person?

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.460
What's your point, Meg?

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:30.560
My point is that with all the irresponsible,
reckless, idiotic behavior in your past, that

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:36.710
somehow, somehow you have the nerve, the
arrogance to consistently and ruthlessly

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:38.450
point out my shortcomings.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.200
All right. Well, fine. Okay. I'm not the
perfect mother. Who is?

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:46.850
Oh, not only are you not the perfect mother,
you're the furthest thing from.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:53.330
From the moment you gave birth to me, I had to trust
you. I had no choice. I needed you to protect

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:58.130
me from the world, to- to be my guide. To help
me navigate the difficult, confusing and

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.630
vulnerable journey to becoming a person.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:03.750
You have done none of those things.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:09.300
You're my mother, and you took a child's trust and
smashed it into bits in a 17 year long

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:14.340
mission to destroy something that you killed
a long time ago. And honestly, when I turn

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.730
18, I don't know that I ever want to see you
again.

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:26.480
Oh, wow. Everybody's already tweeting "Stewie
just said that".

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:26.980
Oh.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:28.250
You're right.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:34.370
You're right. I'm a terrible mother. I'm so
sorry. I'm so, so sorry.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.010
Meg, can you ever forgive me?

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.270
Oh, God.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:44.660
And you never let Dad stir the paint anymore.
Whatever that means.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:47.120
I didn't know you knew that, Meg, but I'm
glad you brought it up.

